  ('dis-17', 'Constipation', 'constipation', 'Dyschezia / Constipation', '[\"Vibandha\"]', 'Digestive Disorders', 'Gastrointestinal Imbalances', 'Infrequent or difficult bowel movements, classified as Vibandha in Ayurveda, driven by dry Vata dosha.', 'In Ayurveda, Constipation is called Vibandha. It is a classic Vata dosha disorder where the dryness (Rooksha Guna) of Vata absorbs moisture from the colon (Pakwashaya), drying the stool and blocking its downward passage (Apana Vayu obstruction).', '[\"Low intake of water and dietary fiber\",\"Consuming dry, cold, and light snacks\",\"Lack of physical activity\",\"Suppression of natural bowel urges\"]', '[\"Difficult or painful bowel movements\",\"Hard, dry stools\",\"Feeling of incomplete evacuation\",\"Stomach bloating and mild pain\"]', '[\"Irregular daily bowels\",\"Stool hardness\"]', '[\"Hemorrhoids (Piles)\",\"Anal fissures\",\"Severe abdominal cramps\"]', '[\"Aging (increased Vata)\",\"Sedentary routine\",\"Pregnancy\",\"Low fiber fast-food diet\"]', '[\"Hemorrhoids\",\"Anal Fissures\",\"Fecal Impaction\"]', '[\"Drink plenty of warm fluids\",\"Consume fiber-rich cooked foods\",\"Never ignore bowel calls\"]', '[\"Drink warm water with 1 tsp Ghee at bedtime\",\"Consume soaked prunes or figs in morning\"]', 'Mild herbal laxatives (Mridu Rechana) like Triphala, lubricating enemas (Anuvasana Basti), and dietary lubrication with ghee.', 'Fiber supplements, stool softeners, osmotic laxatives, and increased physical activity.', '[\"Haritaki (Terminalia chebula)\",\"Senna\",\"Amalaki\",\"Castor Oil (Eranda Taila)\"]', '[\"Triphala Churna\",\"Gandharvahastadi Castor Oil\",\"Abhayarishta\"]', '[\"Ripe papaya\",\"Warm vegetable soups\",\"Mashed rice with Ghee\",\"Whole grains\",\"Warm milk\"]', '[\"Dry crackers and popcorn\",\"Cold raw salads\",\"White flour (Maida)\",\"Unripe bananas\",\"Excessive tea\"]', '[\"Pawanmuktasana\",\"Malasana (Squat pose)\",\"Vajrasana\"]', '[\"Daily walking (30 mins)\",\"Abdominal wall contractions\"]', 'Wake up early, drink a glass of warm water immediately, and sit in a squatting posture to encourage natural elimination.', '7-8 hours of sleep; late nights aggravate dry Vata.', 'Mindfulness and relaxation techniques.', '[\"Vata\"]', '[\"Colon\",\"Rectum\",\"Digestive System\"]', 'All', 'All', 1, 0, 'Low', 'Varies by individual (typically 3-7 days with dietary changes)', 'If constipation is sudden, severe, accompanied by vomiting or blood in stool.', 'Severe abdominal distension accompanied by inability to pass gas or stool, indicating bowel obstruction.', 93, '[{\"answer\":\"Ghee is highly lubricating (Snigdha) and warm milk pacifies Vata. Together, they soothe the dry colon wall, softening the stool passage.\",\"question\":\"Why does Ghee with warm milk help constipation?\"},{\"answer\":\"Yes, Triphala is a gentle colon toner rather than a habit-forming stimulant laxative. It is safe under professional Vaidya guidelines.\",\"question\":\"Is Triphala safe to take long-term?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Chikitsa Sthana\",\"Sushruta Samhita\",\"American Gastroenterological Association Guidelines\"]', 'Gastroenterologist', '[\"ibs\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519494026892-80bbd2d6fd0d?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519494026892-80bbd2d6fd0d?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.80', 310, 60, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-18', 'Fatty Liver', 'fatty-liver', 'Nonalcoholic Fatty Liver Disease (NAFLD)', '[\"Yakrit Roga\",\"Medo-Vriddhi in Yakrit\"]', 'Lifestyle Diseases', 'Hepatobiliary Disorders', 'Excess fat accumulation in liver cells, understood as Medo-Vriddhi in Yakrit (liver), involving Kapha-Pitta.', 'In Ayurveda, Fatty Liver represents a Kapha-Pitta metabolic imbalance in the liver (Yakrit). Excessive heavy, fat-rich foods slow down the liver\'s fire (Yakrit Agni), causing lipid buildup (Meda) in liver cells and blocking channels of bile excretion.', '[\"High calorie junk food diet\",\"Sedentary lifestyle and obesity\",\"Excessive intake of alcohol or processed sugar\",\"Chronic metabolic dysfunction\"]', '[\"Vague pain in upper right abdomen\",\"Chronic fatigue and weakness\",\"Loss of appetite\",\"Mild bloating after meals\"]', '[\"Slight heavy feeling in abdomen\",\"Occasional nausea\"]', '[\"Jaundice (yellow skin/eyes)\",\"Abdominal swelling (Ascites)\",\"Liver cirrhosis\"]', '[\"Obesity\",\"Type 2 Diabetes\",\"High cholesterol\",\"Sedentary habits\"]', '[\"Nonalcoholic Steatohepatitis (NASH)\",\"Liver Cirrhosis\",\"Liver Failure\"]', '[\"Follow a low fat, high fiber Pitta-Kapha diet\",\"Exercise daily to burn lipids\",\"Limit alcohol and chemical drugs\"]', '[\"Drink warm water with organic turmeric powder morning\",\"Consume fresh amla juice daily\"]', 'Bitter-tonic liver stimulants (Yakrit Uttejak), mild purgatives (Virechana) to clear bile pathways, and fat-burning therapies.', 'Weight loss, healthy diet, avoidance of alcohol, and management of diabetes/cholesterol.', '[\"Bhumyamalaki (Phyllanthus niruri)\",\"Katuki (Picrorhiza kurroa)\",\"Kalmegh\",\"Haridra (Turmeric)\"]', '[\"Arogyavardhini Vati\",\"Liv.52 DS\",\"Punarnavadi Mandoor\"]', '[\"Barley and millets\",\"Bitter gourd\",\"Amla\",\"Leafy green vegetables\",\"Papaya\"]', '[\"Refined sugar and high fructose corn syrup\",\"Deep fried oils\",\"Alcohol\",\"Heavy dairy\",\"Red meat\"]', '[\"Ardha Matsyendrasana\",\"Kapalbhati Pranayama\",\"Mayurasana\"]', '[\"Cardio exercise (running/swimming) 45 mins\",\"Strength training\"]', 'Eat warm, bitter-spiced foods, avoid sleeping in the day, and drink warm lemon water on waking.', '7 hours of night sleep; avoid daytime naps which store liver fat.', 'Regular walking and meditation.', '[\"Kapha\",\"Pitta\"]', '[\"Liver (Yakrit)\",\"Digestive System\"]', 'Adults', 'All', 0, 0, 'Moderate', 'Varies by individual (typically 3-6 months for reversal with lifestyle change)', 'If ultrasound shows Grade 2 or 3 fatty liver, or liver enzymes (SGOT/SGPT) are highly elevated.', 'Severe yellowing of eyes/skin, vomiting blood, or sudden severe confusion (hepatic encephalopathy).', 88, '[{\"answer\":\"Bhumyamalaki is highly hepatoprotective. It regenerates liver cells, regulates enzymes, and reduces fat accumulation by cooling Pitta and clearing Kapha.\",\"question\":\"How does Bhumyamalaki help the liver?\"},{\"answer\":\"Yes, Grade 1 Fatty Liver is completely reversible with dietary changes, regular exercise, and liver-stimulating Ayurvedic herbs within 2-3 months.\",\"question\":\"Can Grade 1 Fatty Liver be reversed?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Chikitsa Sthana\",\"Bhaijajya Ratnavali\",\"American Association for the Study of Liver Diseases\"]', 'Hepatologist', '[\"obesity\",\"diabetes\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519494026892-80bbd2d6fd0d?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519494026892-80bbd2d6fd0d?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.80', 490, 120, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-19', 'Gout', 'gout', 'Gouty Arthritis', '[\"Vatarakta\",\"Adhyavata\"]', 'Bone & Joints', 'Joint & Skeletal Imbalances', 'A form of inflammatory arthritis causing severe joint pain due to uric acid crystals, known as Vatarakta in Ayurveda.', 'In Ayurveda, Gout is known as Vatarakta. It is caused by aggravated Vata dosha combined with vitiated blood (Rakta Dhatu). The blood impurities block Vata\'s path, causing it to pool in the small joints (like the big toe) and crystallize, producing severe pain and redness.', '[\"High intake of red meat, seafood, and alcohol\",\"Suppression of natural urges\",\"Irregular sleeping patterns\",\"Trauma to small joints\"]', '[\"Sudden, severe joint pain (usually big toe)\",\"Joint swelling, redness, and warmth\",\"Extreme tenderness (even a sheet hurts)\",\"Limited joint movement\"]', '[\"Mild throbbing in big toe joint at night\",\"Slight warmth in joint\"]', '[\"Tophi (visible chalky joint lumps)\",\"Chronic joint deformity\",\"Kidney stones\"]', '[\"High purine diet\",\"Alcohol abuse\",\"Obesity\",\"Family history of gout\"]', '[\"Tophi formation\",\"Joint destruction\",\"Urate kidney stones\"]', '[\"Limit high-purine foods\",\"Stay hydrated (flush uric acid)\",\"Avoid alcohol, especially beer\"]', '[\"Apply paste of organic turmeric and ginger on joint\",\"Drink water boiled with Giloy stem\"]', 'Bloodletting (Raktamokshana) to relieve acute pain, blood-purifying herbs (Giloy/Kaishore Guggulu), and Vata-pacifying cooling therapies.', 'Colchicine, NSAIDs, corticosteroids, and xanthine oxidase inhibitors (Allopurinol) to lower uric acid.', '[\"Guduchi / Giloy (Tinospora cordifolia)\",\"Manjistha\",\"Kaishore Guggulu\",\"Shallaki\"]', '[\"Kaishore Guggulu\",\"Guduchi Ghana Vati\",\"Pinda Taila (for application)\"]', '[\"Fresh cherries\",\"Bottle gourd and pumpkin\",\"Barley\",\"Green gram (Mung dal)\",\"Coconut water\"]', '[\"Red meat and organ meat\",\"Seafood and shellfish\",\"Alcohol (especially beer)\",\"Sour curd and pickles\",\"Spinach and mushrooms\"]', '[\"Sukshma Vyayama\",\"Tadasana\",\"Pranayama (Nadi Shodhana)\"]', '[\"Gentle joint movements (avoid during acute flares)\"]', 'Drink warm water, apply cooling Pinda Taila on painful joints, and take blood-purifying herbs regularly.', '7-8 hours of sleep; avoid sleeping in late which increases Vatarakta.', 'Calming meditation and gentle breathing.', '[\"Vata\",\"Pitta\"]', '[\"Small Joints\",\"Big Toe\",\"Blood (Rakta)\"]', 'Adults', 'All', 1, 0, 'High', 'Varies by individual (typically 1-3 weeks for acute flare resolution)', 'If joint pain is accompanied by high fever or if joint skin breaks open.', 'High fever with chills and a hot, swollen joint, indicating septic arthritis (joint infection risk).', 86, '[{\"answer\":\"Giloy is a unique herb that purifies blood, balances both Vata and Pitta doshas, and supports the kidneys in filtering uric acid crystals.\",\"question\":\"Why Giloy (Guduchi) is the main herb in Gout?\"},{\"answer\":\"Yes, beer is high in purines (yeast content) and dehydrates the body, making it a double trigger for acute gout attacks.\",\"question\":\"Is beer worse than other alcohol for gout?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Chikitsa Sthana (Vatarakta Chikitsa)\",\"Madhava Nidana\",\"American College of Rheumatology Gout Guidelines\"]', 'Rheumatologist', '[\"arthritis\",\"kidney-stones\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559839734-2b71ea197ec2?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559839734-2b71ea197ec2?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.80', 340, 80, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-2', 'PCOS', 'pcos', 'Polycystic ovary syndrome', '[\"Artava Srotas Roga\",\"Pushpagni Vandhyatva\"]', 'Women\'s Health', 'Gynecological Imbalances', 'A common hormonal disorder in women of reproductive age, characterized by irregular cycles and ovarian cysts, linked to Kapha-Vata imbalances.', 'In Ayurveda, PCOS originates from an accumulation of Kapha and Vata doshas in the reproductive channels (Artava Srotas). This creates blockages, leading to cyst formation (Granthi) in the ovaries, sluggish tissue metabolism (Dhatu Agnimandya), and hormonal stagnation.', '[\"Excessive intake of cold, sweet, and heavy foods\",\"Sedentary lifestyle and lack of physical exercise\",\"Chronic emotional stress\",\"Irregular sleep patterns\"]', '[\"Irregular menstrual cycles\",\"Excess facial and body hair (Hirsutism)\",\"Weight gain particularly around the abdomen\",\"Cystic acne\",\"Thinning scalp hair\"]', '[\"Slightly prolonged cycles\",\"Mild pelvic discomfort\",\"Occasional mood swings\"]', '[\"Absent periods (Amenorrhea)\",\"Infertility issues\",\"Severe insulin resistance\"]', '[\"Family history of PCOS\",\"Obesity\",\"Poor dietary habits\",\"High stress levels\"]', '[\"Infertility\",\"Type 2 Diabetes\",\"Endometrial hyperplasia\",\"Depression\"]', '[\"Follow a Vata-Kapha balancing diet\",\"Engage in active daily movement\",\"Limit processed dairy and sweets\"]', '[\"Drink warm sesame and cumin water morning\",\"Consume cinnamon powder with warm water\"]', 'Cleansing therapies like Virechana and Uttar Basti (specialized medicated enemas) to clear pelvic channel blockages, combined with hormone-balancing herbs.', 'Oral contraceptive pills, Metformin for insulin resistance, anti-androgen medicines, and weight loss counseling.', '[\"Shatavari (Asparagus racemosus)\",\"Kanchnar Guggulu\",\"Ashoka bark\",\"Aloe Vera\"]', '[\"Chandraprabha Vati\",\"Raja Pravartini Vati\",\"Kanchnar Guggulu\"]', '[\"Fresh papaya\",\"Sprouted legumes\",\"Leafy green vegetables\",\"Whole grains like ragi\",\"Sesame seeds\"]', '[\"Cold dairy products\",\"Refined flour (Maida)\",\"Deep fried foods\",\"Red meat\",\"Refined white sugar\"]', '[\"Badha Konasana (Butterfly pose)\",\"Surya Namaskar\",\"Supta Badha Konasana\"]', '[\"Moderate aerobics\",\"Strength training (3-4 times a week)\",\"Yoga\"]', 'Ensure dinner is light and consumed before 7 PM, sleep by 10:30 PM, and maintain consistent waking times.', '7-8 hours of sound sleep; avoid sleeping during the daytime.', 'Meditation, deep breathing (Pranayama), and outdoor walks in nature.', '[\"Kapha\",\"Vata\"]', '[\"Ovaries\",\"Uterus\",\"Endocrine System\"]', 'Adults', 'Female', 0, 0, 'Moderate', 'Varies by individual and severity (typically 3-6 months)', 'If periods are missed for more than 3 consecutive months, or if you face difficulty conceiving.', 'Severe, sudden lower abdominal pain (ovarian cyst rupture risk) or heavy prolonged bleeding.', 88, '[{\"answer\":\"Yes, by clearing metabolic blockages in the ovaries and balancing Apana Vayu (the downward flow of energy), Ayurveda restores natural ovulation and cycle regularity.\",\"question\":\"Can Ayurveda restore regular cycles in PCOS?\"},{\"answer\":\"Yes, reducing or stopping heavy dairy (especially cold cheese, paneer, and curd) is recommended, as it causes blockage (Abhishyandi) in reproductive channels.\",\"question\":\"Do I need to stop all dairy?\"}]', '[\"Ashtanga Hridaya Sharira Sthana\",\"Bhavaprakasha Samhita\",\"Modern Endocrinology Research\"]', 'Gynecologist', '[\"diabetes\",\"obesity\",\"anxiety\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518152006812-edab29b069ac?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518152006812-edab29b069ac?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.70', 480, 140, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-20', 'Chronic Fatigue', 'chronic-fatigue', 'Myalgic Encephalomyelitis (ME/CFS)', '[\"Klama\",\"Ojas-Kshaya\"]', 'Mental Wellness', 'Energy & Nervous Imbalances', 'Persistent unexplained fatigue not relieved by rest, matching Klama or depletion of vital energy (Ojas) in Ayurveda.', 'In Ayurveda, Chronic Fatigue is understood as Klama (fatigue without exertion) or Ojas-Kshaya (depletion of vital life force). It occurs when poor digestion (Mandagni) produces chronic toxins (Ama) that coat body tissues, preventing nutrition from reaching the cells and depleting Ojas.', '[\"Chronic mental stress and emotional trauma\",\"Irregular lifestyle and sleep deprivation\",\"Eating nutrient-depleted stale foods\",\"Undiagnosed chronic infections\"]', '[\"Severe fatigue lasting more than 6 months\",\"Post-exertional malaise (PEM)\",\"Unrefreshing sleep\",\"Muscle and joint pain without swelling\",\"Brain fog and memory issues\"]', '[\"Mild low energy in mornings\",\"Frequent body aches\"]', '[\"Severe physical weakness (bedridden)\",\"Extreme light/sound sensitivity\",\"Orthostatic intolerance (dizziness when standing)\"]', '[\"High stress profession\",\"History of viral infections\",\"Vata-heavy constitution\",\"Poor nutrition\"]', '[\"Social withdrawal\",\"Depression due to physical limitations\",\"Chronic muscle wasting\"]', '[\"Follow a warm, nourishing Sattvik diet\",\"Maintain regular rest-activity cycles\",\"Engage in gentle daily meditation\"]', '[\"Drink warm almond-ashwagandha milk daily\",\"Eat fresh dates and raisins soaked overnight\"]', 'Gentle toxin-clearing herbs, digestive fire stimulation, followed by deep rejuvenation therapy (Rasayana) to rebuild Ojas.', 'Symptom management, pacing/activity management, sleep support, and cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT) support.', '[\"Ashwagandha (Withania somnifera)\",\"Shatavari\",\"Brahmi\",\"Yashtimadhu\"]', '[\"Chyawanprash\",\"Ashwagandharishta\",\"Balarishta\"]', '[\"Fresh sweet fruits\",\"Cow\'s Ghee\",\"Almond milk\",\"Sprouted green gram\",\"Cooked whole grains\"]', '[\"Canned and frozen foods\",\"Cold carbonated drinks\",\"Refined flour and white sugar\",\"Leftover stale food\",\"Excessive caffeine\"]', '[\"Shavasana\",\"Bhramari Pranayama\",\"Viparita Karani (Legs-up-the-wall pose)\"]', '[\"Extremely gentle stretching (pacing is critical, avoid overexertion)\"]', 'Follow a gentle dinacharya, perform mild self-Abhyanga with sesame oil, eat warm fresh meals, and sleep by 10 PM.', '8-9 hours of sound sleep; ensure a peaceful, dark bedroom.', 'Mindful breathing and emotional release exercises.', '[\"Vata\",\"Kapha\"]', '[\"Nervous System\",\"Brain\",\"Vital Energy (Ojas)\"]', 'All', 'All', 1, 0, 'Moderate', 'Varies by individual (typically 3-12 months for energy restoration)', 'If fatigue is accompanied by unexplained weight loss, night sweats, or swollen lymph nodes.', 'Severe chest pain, sudden difficulty breathing, or severe suicidal thoughts due to chronic debility.', 84, '[{\"answer\":\"Ojas is the vital essence of all seven bodily tissues. It represents ultimate immunity, physical strength, mental stability, and radiant energy.\",\"question\":\"What is Ojas in Ayurveda?\"},{\"answer\":\"In CFS, cell energy production is impaired. Ayurveda views this as Ojas depletion. Push-through exercise drains the remaining vitality, leading to crashes.\",\"question\":\"Why does exercise make CFS worse?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Sutra Sthana (Ojas Sthana)\",\"Ashtanga Hridaya\",\"Institute of Medicine CFS Diagnostic Criteria\"]', 'Ayurveda Rejuvenation Specialist', '[\"anxiety\",\"insomnia\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540555700478-4be289fbecef?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540555700478-4be289fbecef?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.70', 310, 85, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-21', 'Sinusitis', 'sinusitis', 'Sinusitis', '[\"Pinasa\",\"Dustha Pratishyaya\"]', 'Respiratory Disorders', 'Pulmonary Imbalances', 'Sinus lining inflammation causing nasal blockage, understood as Pinasa in Ayurveda, involving Kapha-Vata.', 'In Ayurveda, Sinusitis is called Pinasa or Dustha Pratishyaya. It is caused by aggravated Kapha and Vata doshas. Cold draft exposure and slow digestion create thick mucus that blocks the nasal cavities (Sinus channels), leading to pressure and headaches.', '[\"Exposure to cold damp weather\",\"High intake of cold dairy and heavy sweets\",\"Dust and allergen inhalation\",\"Inadequate sleep\"]', '[\"Facial pain and pressure\",\"Nasal congestion and thick yellow discharge\",\"Headache (worse when bending forward)\",\"Loss of smell\"]', '[\"Sneezing\",\"Runny nose\",\"Heavy head\"]', '[\"Severe facial swelling\",\"High fever\",\"Tooth pain\"]', '[\"Allergies\",\"Nasal polyps\",\"Weak immunity\",\"Cold drinks intake\"]', '[\"Chronic sinusitis\",\"Orbital cellulitis\",\"Meningitis (very rare)\"]', '[\"Inhale steam regularly\",\"Avoid cold drinks\",\"Keep head covered in cold weather\"]', '[\"Drink warm ginger-basil tea\",\"Inhale steam with mint leaves\"]', 'Nasya therapy (nasal drops) to clear mucus, facial massage, steam inhalation, and Kapha-reducing warming herbs.', 'Nasal saline rinses, decongestants, nasal corticosteroid sprays, and antibiotics if bacterial.', '[\"Tulsi (Ocimum sanctum)\",\"Ginger\",\"Haridra (Turmeric)\",\"Pippali\"]', '[\"Chitrak Haritaki\",\"Anu Taila\",\"Laxmivilas Ras\"]', '[\"Warm soups\",\"Ginger-infused hot water\",\"Spicy vegetables\",\"Rice with cumin\"]', '[\"Ice cream and cold curd\",\"Cold water\",\"Bananas\",\"Heavy fried foods\"]', '[\"Jala Neti (Nasal cleansing)\",\"Bhastrika Pranayama\",\"Adho Mukha Svanasana\"]', '[\"Gentle walking\"]', 'Perform Jala Neti or steam inhalation every morning, drink warm water, and avoid head wash in late evenings.', '7-8 hours; sleep with head elevated.', 