  ('dis-24', 'Sciatica', 'sciatica', 'Sciatica', '[\"Gridhrasi\"]', 'Bone & Joints', 'Joint & Skeletal Imbalances', 'Pain radiating along the sciatic nerve path, classified as Gridhrasi in Ayurveda, caused by aggravated Vata dosha.', 'In Ayurveda, Sciatica is called Gridhrasi (vulture-like gait). It occurs when aggravated Vata dosha inflames or compresses the sciatic nerve at the lower back (Kati), causing sharp radiating pain, stiffness, and weakness down the leg.', '[\"Lifting heavy weights incorrectly\",\"Sitting for long hours on hard chairs\",\"Exposure to cold dry drafts\",\"Underlying herniated disc\"]', '[\"Radiating pain from lower back to heel\",\"Numbness and tingling in leg\",\"Stiffness and difficulty walking\",\"Shooting pain when coughing or sitting\"]', '[\"Mild backache\",\"Occasional shooting thigh pain\"]', '[\"Loss of leg muscle strength\",\"Inability to flex foot (foot drop)\",\"Loss of bowel control (rare emergency)\"]', '[\"Sedentary desk job\",\"Aging (Vata stage of life)\",\"Obesity\",\"Heavy manual labor\"]', '[\"Permanent nerve damage\",\"Muscle wasting in leg\"]', '[\"Maintain good posture\",\"Use lumbar support while sitting\",\"Avoid sudden jerking back movements\"]', '[\"Massage leg with warm Mahanarayan oil\",\"Incorporate garlic in diet (Vata-pacifying)\"]', 'Local oil pooling (Kati Basti), herbal leaf poultice steaming (Patra Pinda Sweda), and medicated oil enemas (Basti) to nourish the lower spine.', 'Physical therapy, pain relievers, epidural steroid injections, and discectomy surgery in severe cases.', '[\"Nirgundi\",\"Shallaki\",\"Garlic (Lashuna)\",\"Guggulu\"]', '[\"Yograj Guggulu\",\"Maharasnadi Kadha\",\"Trayodashang Guggulu\"]', '[\"Warm, oily, and sweet foods\",\"Ghee\",\"Garlic-cooked soups\",\"Root vegetables\",\"Hot milk\"]', '[\"Dry snacks and cold salads\",\"Ice-cold drinks\",\"White flour\",\"Nightshade vegetables\"]', '[\"Bhujangasana (Cobra pose)\",\"Shalabhasana\",\"Pawanmuktasana (gentle variant)\"]', '[\"Gentle 