  ('dis-25', 'Piles', 'piles', 'Hemorrhoids', '[\"Arsha\"]', 'Digestive Disorders', 'Gastrointestinal Imbalances', 'Swollen veins in the anus and lower rectum, known as Arsha in Ayurveda, caused by slow digestive fire.', 'In Ayurveda, Piles are called Arsha. It is considered a digestive disorder originating from weak digestive fire (Mandagni) and chronic constipation (Vibandha). Aggravated Vata-Pitta doshas accumulate in rectal vessels, causing local swelling and bleeding.', '[\"Chronic constipation and straining during bowel movements\",\"High intake of dry, spicy, and junk foods\",\"Sitting for long hours on hard seats\",\"Lack of physical exercise\"]', '[\"Painless bleeding during bowel movements\",\"Itching or irritation in anal region\",\"Pain or discomfort while sitting\",\"Lumps around the anus\"]', '[\"Occasional blood drops on toilet tissue\",\"Mild anal itching\"]', '[\"Prolapsed internal hemorrhoids\",\"Severe throbbing rectal pain\",\"Chronic anemia due to bleeding\"]', '[\"Obesity\",\"Pregnancy\",\"Low fiber diet\",\"Chronic diarrhea or constipation\"]', '[\"Strangulated hemorrhoid\",\"Anemia due to chronic blood loss\",\"Thrombosed hemorrhoid\"]', '[\"Eat high-fiber foods\",\"Drink plenty of water\",\"Avoid sitting for long hours\"]', '[\"Sit in a warm sitz bath with triphala decoction\",\"Drink buttermilk infused with Haritaki\"]', 'Stool-softening herbs, sitz baths, and specialized minimally invasive thread therapy (Kshar Sutra) for advanced hemorrhoids.', 'Rubber band ligation, sclerotherapy, and hemorrhoidectomy surgery.', '[\"Haritaki\",\"Suran (Elephant Foot Yam)\",\"Giloy\",\"Neem\"]', '[\"Abhayarishta\",\"Arshoghni Vati\",\"Triphala Guggulu\"]', '[\"Elephant foot yam\",\"Papaya\",\"Buttermilk churned with cumin\",\"Oatmeal\",\"Warm soups\"]', '[\"Spicy chillies and pickles\",\"Deep fried foods\",\"Dry crunchy snacks\",\"Refined flour\",\"Caffeine\"]', '[\"Malasana (Squating)\",\"Pawanmuktasana\",\"Viparita Karani\"]', '[\"Kegel exercises\",\"Gentle walking\"]', 'Drink warm water morning, sit on soft cushions, avoid straining at toilet, and consume freshly churned buttermilk daily.', '7-8 hours; avoid sleeping late.', 'Calming yoga.', '[\"Vata\",\"Pitta\"]', '[\"Rectum\",\"Anal Canal\",\"Digestive System\"]', 'All', 'All', 0, 0, 'Moderate', 'Varies by individual (typically 2-4 weeks with dietary management)', 'If bleeding is heavy, persistent, or accompanied by severe anal pain.', 'Dizziness, fainting, or pale skin due to sudden, excessive rectal bleeding.', 88, '[{\"answer\":\"Suran is highly Vata-pacifying, stool-softening, and has specific properties to shrink rectal blood vessel swelling, making it the premier food-medicine for Arsha.\",\"question\":\"Why is Suran (Yam) recommended in Piles?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Chikitsa Sthana (Arsha Chikitsa)\",\"Madhava Nidana\"]', 'Proctologist', '[\"constipation\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519494026892-80bbd2d6fd0d?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519494026892-80bbd2d6fd0d?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.80', 450, 95, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-26', 'Indigestion', 'indigestion', 'Dyspepsia', '[\"Ajeerna\"]', 'Digestive Disorders', 'Gastrointestinal Imbalances', 'Discomfort or bloating in the upper abdomen, known as Ajeerna in Ayurveda, caused by weak digestive Agni.', 'In Ayurveda, Indigestion is called Ajeerna. It is the root cause of all physical diseases. It occurs when the digestive fire (Agni) becomes weak or erratic, failing to digest food properly and generating raw toxins (Ama) that clog body channels.', '[\"Overeating or eating before previous meal is digested\",\"Consuming incompatible food combinations\",\"Drinking ice-cold water during meals\",\"Eating during anger, anxiety, or stress\"]', '[\"Feeling of fullness during/after meals\",\"Bloating and gas in the stomach\",\"Mild upper abdominal pain\",\"Nausea and acid burps\",\"Loss of appetite\"]', '[\"Slight heaviness in stomach after eating\",\"Irregular appetite\"]', '[\"Vomiting raw food\",\"Diarrhea with undigested particles\",\"Systemic body fatigue (due to Ama)\"]', '[\"Stressful eating environment\",\"Irregular food habits\",\"High intake of junk food\",\"Lack of sleep\"]', '[\"Chronic toxin buildup (Ama)\",\"IBS\",\"Nutritional deficiencies\"]', '[\"Eat only when hungry\",\"Chew food properly\",\"Avoid drinking cold water with meals\"]', '[\"Chew slice of fresh ginger with rock salt before meals\",\"Drink warm fennel water\"]', 'Fast (Langhana) to digest raw toxins, intake of Agni-stimulating spices (Deepana-Pachana), and colon-cleansing herbs.', 'H2 blockers, PPIs, prokinetics, and dietary changes.', '[\"Ginger (Sunthi)\",\"Pippali\",\"Cumin\",\"Hing (Asafoetida)\"]', '[\"Trikatu Churna\",\"Chitrakadi Vati\",\"Lavan Bhaskar Churna\"]', '[\"Warm mung dal soup\",\"Pomegranate\",\"Buttermilk with cumin\",\"Roasted cumin water\",\"Boiled rice\"]', '[\"Cold raw salads\",\"Heavy fried foods\",\"Sweets and heavy dairy\",\"Processed bakery items\",\"Ice water\"]', '[\"Vajrasana (immediately after meals)\",\"Pavanamuktasana\",\"Paschimottanasana\"]', '[\"Light walking (100 steps after meals)\"]', 'Eat meals at consistent times, avoid distractions like phone or TV during meals, and drink warm water throughout the day.', '7-8 hours; do not sleep immediately after eating.', 'Mindfulness and calm eating practices.', '[\"Vata\",\"Kapha\",\"Pitta\"]', '[\"Stomach\",\"Duodenum\",\"Small Intestine\"]', 'All', 'All', 1, 0, 'Low', 'Varies by individual (typically 1-3 days for acute episodes)', 'If indigestion is accompanied by unexplained weight loss, persistent vomiting, or difficulty swallowing.', 'Sudden severe abdominal pain, chest pain radiating to arm, or vomiting blood.', 94, '[{\"answer\":\"Ice-cold water dampens the digestive fire (Agni), similar to pouring cold water on burning firewood. It stops enzyme secretion and causes food to ferment.\",\"question\":\"Why is drinking ice water bad during meals?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Sutra Sthana\",\"Madhava Nidana\"]', 'Gastroenterologist', '[\"gastritis\",\"ibs\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519494026892-80bbd2d6fd0d?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519494026892-80bbd2d6fd0d?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.90', 520, 80, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-27', 'Allergic Rhinitis', 'allergic-rhinitis', 'Allergic Rhinitis', '[\"Vata-Kapha Pratishyaya\"]', 'Respiratory Disorders', 'Pulmonary Imbalances', 'Immune reaction to allergens causing sneezing and runny nose, understood as Vata-Kapha Pratishyaya in Ayurveda.', 'In Ayurveda, Allergic Rhinitis is called Vata-Kapha Pratishyaya. It is a disorder where Vata and Kapha doshas accumulate in the nasal cavities due to exposure to cold, dust, or allergens. It is exacerbated by weak digestion which generates toxins (Ama) that trigger hyper-immunity.', '[\"Inhalation of dust, pollen, and pet dander\",\"Exposure to cold drafty weather or AC\",\"Consuming cold dairy and heavy sweets\",\"Weak underlying immunity (Ojas)\"]', '[\"Frequent sneezing fit (especially in morning)\",\"Runny nose with clear watery discharge\",\"Itchy eyes, nose, and throat\",\"Nasal congestion and heavy head\"]', '[\"Mild tickling in throat/nose\",\"Watery eyes\"]', '[\"Loss of sense of smell\",\"Sinus headaches\",\"Asthma flare-ups\"]', '[\"Allergy history\",\"AC environments\",\"High consumption of cold foods\",\"Dusty occupations\"]', '[\"Chronic sinusitis\",\"Nasal polyps\",\"Middle ear infections\"]', '[\"Avoid direct exposure to dust/pollen\",\"Drink warm ginger water\",\"Avoid cold AC drafts on face\"]', '[\"Drink turmeric milk with black pepper\",\"Inhale steam with basil oil\"]', 'Nasya therapy (oil drops) to lubricate nasal lining, digestive herbs to burn Ama, and immuno-modulating herbs (Rasayana).', 'Antihistamines, nasal corticosteroid sprays, decongestants, and immunotherapy.', '[\"Haridra (Turmeric)\",\"Tulsi\",\"Pippali\",\"Guduchi\"]', '[\"Haridra Khanda\",\"Anu Taila (for Nasya)\",\"Trikatu Churna\"]', '[\"Warm vegetable soups\",\"Spiced hot water\",\"Rice with black pepper\",\"Leafy greens\"]', '[\"Ice creams and cold water\",\"Yoghurt and cheese\",\"Bananas and citrus\",\"Fermented foods\"]', '[\"Jala Neti\",\"Anulom Vilom Pranayama\",\"Kapalbhati\"]', '[\"Light aerobic exercise\"]', 'Apply Anu Taila in nostrils daily, drink warm water, and avoid cold water head wash in the mornings.', '7-8 hours; sleep in a dust-free bedroom.', 'Deep breathing relaxation.', '[\"Vata\",\"Kapha\"]', '[\"Nose\",\"Sinuses\",\"Respiratory Tract\"]', 'All', 'All', 1, 0, 'Low', 'Varies by individual (typically 1-3 weeks for acute symptom reduction)', 'If allergy symptoms are constant, interfere with sleep, or lead to facial pressure.', 'Sudden onset of severe breathlessness or swelling of lips/throat (anaphylaxis).', 88, '[{\"answer\":\"Haridra Khanda is a classical formulation with Turmeric as the main ingredient. It acts as a systemic anti-allergic and immunomodulator, reducing nasal hypersensitivity.\",\"question\":\"How does Haridra Khanda help in allergies?\"}]', '[\"Sushruta Samhita Uttara Tantra\",\"Ashtanga Hridaya\"]', 'Allergist', '[\"asthma\",\"sinusitis\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559839734-2b71ea197ec2?w=400&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559839734-2b71ea197ec2?w=400&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.80', 340, 70, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-28', 'Osteoporosis', 'osteoporosis', 'Osteoporosis', '[\"Asthi Saushirya\"]', 'Bone & Joints', 'Joint & Skeletal Imbalances', 'Bone weakening disease increasing fracture risk, classified as Asthi Saushirya in Ayurveda, driven by high Vata dosha.', 'In Ayurveda, Osteoporosis is known as Asthi Saushirya (porous bones). It is a degenerative disease of the bone tissue (Asthi Dhatu) driven by aggravated Vata dosha. Since Vata\'s seat is in the bones, elevated Vata (due to aging or poor nutrition) dries up bone minerals, making them brittle.', '[\"Aging (natural Vata dominance)\",\"Poor calcium and mineral absorption due to slow Agni\",\"Post-menopausal hormonal changes\",\"Lack of weight-bearing exercises\"]', '[\"Loss of height over time\",\"Stooped posture (dowager\'s hump)\",\"Bone fractures that occur easily\",\"Mild, persistent back pain\"]', '[\"Weak grip strength\",\"Brittle nails\"]', '[\"Vertebral compression fractures\",\"Hip fracture from minor fall\"]', '[\"Post-menopause (women)\",\"Low calcium diet\",\"Sedentary lifestyle\",\"Smoking and alcohol\"]', '[\"Spinal fractures\",\"Loss of mobility\",\"Chronic pain\"]', '[\"Consume calcium-rich foods\",\"Practice weight-bearing exercises\",\"Nourish body with warm oil massages\"]', '[\"Drink warm milk with organic sesame seed powder\",\"Perform self-massage with warm sesame oil daily\"]', 'Medicated oil enemas (Basti) containing bone-nourishing herbs and calcium, combined with systemic oil therapies (Abhyanga) to ground Vata.', 'Bisphosphonates, calcium and Vitamin D supplements, hormone replacement therapy, and bone-strengthening exercises.', '[\"Shallaki\",\"Ashwagandha\",\"Arjuna\",\"Asthisamharaka (Cissus quadrangularis)\"]', '[\"Lakshadi Guggulu\",\"Praval Pishti (coral calcium)\",\"Mukta Pishti\"]', '[\"Sesame seeds\",\"Warm milk with ghee\",\"Ragi (finger millet)\",\"Almonds\",\"Cooked green vegetables\"]', '[\"Dry, light, and cold foods\",\"Carbonated soft drinks (leach calcium)\",\"Excessive caffeine and alcohol\"]', '[\"Tadasana (Mountain pose)\",\"Virabhadrasana (Warrior pose)\",\"Vrikshasana\"]', '[\"Light weight-bearing walking\",\"Resistance band exercises\"]', 'Incorporate sesame oil body massage before bath, sit in mild morning sunlight (Vitamin D), and eat warm, mineral-rich foods.', '7-8 hours; ensure comfortable, warm bedding.', 'Grounding meditation.', '[\"Vata\"]', '[\"Bones (Asthi Dhatu)\",\"Spine\",\"Hip Joints\"]', 'Seniors', 'All', 1, 0, 'High', 'Varies by individual (Management of bone density, typically 6+ months for bone strengthening)', 'If bone density scan (DEXA) shows T-score below -2.5, or after any fracture from a minor fall.', 'Sudden, severe back pain, which may indicate a vertebral compression fracture.', 82, '[{\"answer\":\"Asthisamharaka translates literally to \'that which saves bones\'. It accelerates bone healing, increases osteoblast activity, and supports calcium deposition in bone tissues.\",\"question\":\"Why is Asthisamharaka (Cissus) called bone setter?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Chikitsa Sthana\",\"National Osteoporosis Foundation Guidelines\"]', 'Orthopedic Specialist', '[\"arthritis\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559839734-2b71ea197ec2?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559839734-2b71ea197ec2?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.80', 310, 75, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-29', 'UTI', 'uti', 'Urinary Tract Infection', '[\"Mutrakrichhra\"]', 'Women\'s Health', 'Urinary Tract Imbalances', 'Infection of the urinary system causing burning urination, matching Mutrakrichhra in Ayurveda, driven by Pitta dosha.', 'In Ayurveda, UTI is called Mutrakrichhra (difficulty in urination). It is driven by an aggravated Pitta dosha. Excess body heat and toxic accumulation in the urinary channels (Mutra Vaha Srotas) irritate the bladder lining, causing burning and pain.', '[\"Drinking inadequate water (Dehydration)\",\"Eating excessively spicy, sour, and hot foods\",\"Suppressing the urge to urinate\",\"Improper personal hygiene\"]', '[\"Burning sensation during urination (Daha)\",\"Frequent urge to urinate but small output\",\"Cloudy or strong-smelling urine\",\"Lower abdominal pain\"]', '[\"Mild irritation when passing urine\",\"Increased frequency\"]', '[\"High fever with chills\",\"Blood in urine (Hematuria)\",\"Severe back/kidney pain\"]', '[\"Female anatomy (shorter urethra)\",\"Dehydration\",\"Pregnancy\",\"Diabetes\"]', '[\"Kidney infection (Pyelonephritis)\",\"Recurrent UTIs\",\"Sepsis (rare severe)\"]', '[\"Drink 2-3 liters of water daily\",\"Urinate immediately after intercourse\",\"Avoid spicy hot foods\"]', '[\"Drink coriander seeds water twice daily\",\"Drink fresh cranberry juice (no sugar)\"]', 'Cooling diuretic herbs (Mutral), bladder-cleansing decoctions, and Pitta-soothing diet adjustments.', 'Antibiotic course, hydration, and pain relievers.', '[\"Gokshura (Tribulus terrestris)\",\"Varuna\",\"Punarnava\",\"Coriander\"]', '[\"Chandraprabha Vati\",\"Gokshuradi Guggulu\",\"Punarnavasava\"]', '[\"Coconut water\",\"Barley water\",\"Cucumber\",\"Watermelon\",\"Mung dal soup\"]', '[\"Spicy chillies and garlic\",\"Vinegar and pickles\",\"Citrus fruits\",\"Alcohol and strong tea\"]', '[\"Bhujangasana\",\"Vajrasana\",\"Pranayama (Sheetali)\"]', '[\"Light pelvic stretches\"]', 'Drink a glass of water every hour, maintain strict personal hygiene, wear loose cotton undergarments, and avoid direct sun.', '7-8 hours; avoid sleep deprivation which increases body heat.', 'Cooling breathing exercises.', '[\"Pitta\"]', '[\"Urinary Bladder\",\"Urethra\",\"Kidneys\"]', 'All', 'All', 1, 0, 'Moderate', 'Varies by individual (typically 3-7 days with hydration)', 'If burning persists after 3 days, or if you develop fever, chills, or back pain.', 'High fever accompanied by severe flank (side back) pain, vomiting, or blood in urine, indicating kidney infection.', 90, '[{\"answer\":\"Gokshura is a natural cooling diuretic (Mutral). It increases urine output, washes out bacteria from the urinary tract, and soothes the burning bladder lining.\",\"question\":\"Why is Gokshura recommended for UTI?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Chikitsa Sthana (Mutrakrichhra)\",\"Sushruta Samhita\"]', 'Urologist', '[\"kidney-stones\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518152006812-edab29b069ac?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518152006812-edab29b069ac?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.80', 380, 85, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-3', 'Arthritis', 'arthritis', 'Osteoarthritis / Rheumatoid Arthritis', '[\"Sandhivata\",\"Amavata\"]', 'Bone & Joints', 'Joint & Skeletal Imbalances', 'Joint inflammation and degenerative diseases causing pain and stiffness, understood in Ayurveda as Sandhivata or Amavata.', 'In Ayurveda, arthritis manifests as Sandhivata (Osteoarthritis, caused by aggravated Vata dosha degrading joint cartilage) or Amavata (Rheumatoid Arthritis, caused by toxic Ama accumulation in joint channels due to weak digestive fire).', '[\"Excessive dry, cold, and stale food\",\"Overexertion or trauma to joints\",\"Poor digestion leading to Ama production\",\"Cold and damp weather exposure\"]', '[\"Chronic joint pain\",\"Morning joint stiffness\",\"Joint swelling and tenderness\",\"Reduced range of motion\",\"Fatigue\"]', '[\"Occasional crackling sound in joints (crepitus)\",\"Mild stiffness after rest\"]', '[\"Joint deformities\",\"Persistent pain even at rest\",\"Loss of joint function\"]', '[\"Aging\",\"Obesity\",\"Joint injury\",\"Repetitive joint stress\"]', '[\"Joint degeneration\",\"Chronic mobility loss\",\"Sleep disturbances due to pain\"]', '[\"Regular gentle exercise\",\"Keep joints warm and lubricated\",\"Avoid cold and dry foods\"]', '[\"Drink warm water with grated ginger\",\"Apply warm sesame oil topically\"]', 'Local pooling of medicated oils (Janu Basti), herbal steam (Swedana), and detoxification therapies (Virechana & Basti) to clear Ama and calm Vata.', 'Pain relievers (NSAIDs), physical therapy, corticosteroid injections, and joint replacement surgery.', '[\"Shallaki (Boswellia)\",\"Guggulu (Commiphora mukul)\",\"Nirgundi\",\"Ginger (Sunthi)\"]', '[\"Yograj Guggulu\",\"Maharasnadi Kadha\",\"Mahanarayan Taila\"]', '[\"Warm vegetable soups\",\"Cooked grains with Cow\'s Ghee\",\"Garlic\",\"Ginger\",\"Warm water\"]', '[\"Yoghurt and aged cheese\",\"Nightshade vegetables (potatoes, tomatoes)\",\"Cold salads\",\"White beans\"]', '[\"Sukshma Vyayama (Gentle joint rotations)\",\"Tadasana\",\"Pavanamuktasana\"]', '[\"Swimming\",\"Walking on flat surfaces\",\"Gentle stretching\"]', 'Perform self-massage with warm sesame oil daily before bathing, keep joints covered in cold weather, and sleep under warm covers.', '7-8 hours of warm, comfortable sleep; avoid drafty air conditioning.', 'Deep relaxation techniques, warm baths, and meditation.', '[\"Vata\",\"Kapha\"]', '[\"Joints\",\"Bones\",\"Connective Tissues\"]', 'Seniors', 'All', 1, 0, 'High', 'Varies by individual and severity (typically 3-6 months for relief)', 'If joint swelling becomes severe, hot to the touch, or accompanied by fever.', 'Inability to bear weight on a joint suddenly, indicating acute fracture or joint infection.', 80, '[{\"answer\":\"Ghee acts as a systemic lubricant (Snehana) which pacifies Vata dosha, nourishes joint cartilage, and supports healthy digestion.\",\"question\":\"How does Ghee help in arthritis?\"},{\"answer\":\"Yes, gentle walking on flat surfaces keeps the joints mobile and prevents muscle wasting, but avoid walking during acute pain/inflammation.\",\"question\":\"Is walking good for arthritic knees?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Chikitsa Sthana\",\"Madhava Nidana\",\"Modern Rheumatology Guidelines\"]', 'Ayurveda Joint Specialist', '[\"obesity\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559839734-2b71ea197ec2?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559839734-2b71ea197ec2?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.90', 410, 110, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-30', 'Kidney Stones', 'kidney-stones', 'Nephrolithiasis', '[\"Ashmari\"]', 'Lifestyle Diseases', 'Urinary Tract Imbalances', 'Hard mineral deposits forming in the kidneys, classified as Ashmari in Ayurveda, driven by Vata-Kapha.', 'In Ayurveda, Kidney Stones are called Ashmari (stones). They occur when aggravated Vata dosha dries up urinary chemicals and Kapha dosha binds them together with minerals, forming hard structures in the kidney channels (Mutra Vaha Srotas).', '[\"Inadequate water consumption\",\"Excessive intake of dry, heavy, and astringent foods\",\"High consumption of calcium-oxalate rich foods\",\"Sedentary lifestyle\"]', '[\"Severe, sharp pain in back and side (flank pain)\",\"Pain radiating to lower abdomen and groin\",\"Pain during urination\",\"Pink, red, or brown urine\"]', '[\"Mild backache\",\"Cloudy urine\",\"Slight burning during urination\"]', '[\"Severe renal colic (excruciating pain waves)\",\"Vomiting and nausea\",\"Fever and chills (if infection is present)\"]', '[\"Dehydration\",\"High protein or high sodium diet\",\"Obesity\",\"Family history of stones\"]', '[\"Urinary tract obstruction\",\"Kidney damage due to backup pressure\",\"Recurrent UTIs\"]', '[\"Drink 3+ liters of water daily\",\"Limit dietary sodium and animal proteins\",\"Consume cooling barley water\"]', '[\"Drink banana stem juice in morning\",\"Drink coconut water and horse gram (Kulthi) decoction\"]', 'Stone-dissolving herbs (Ashmarighna), diuretic decoctions to flush channels, and Vata-pacifying cooling oil treatments.', 'Pain relievers, hydration, medical therapy to pass stone (alpha-blockers), and lithotripsy (sound waves to break stones) or surgery.', '[\"Pashanbhed (Bergenia ligulata)\",\"Gokshura\",\"Varuna (Crataeva nurvala)\",\"Punarnava\"]', '[\"Cystone\",\"Chandraprabha Vati\",\"Varunadi Vati\"]', '[\"Horse gram (Kulthi) soup\",\"Barley water\",\"Cucumber\",\"Pomegranate\",\"Coconut water\"]', '[\"Spinach and tomatoes (high oxalate)\",\"Red meat\",\"Excessive salt\",\"Chocolates and nuts\",\"Carbonated beverages\"]', '[\"Pavanamuktasana\",\"Bhujangasana\",\"Dhanurasana\"]', '[\"Regular moderate walking\",\"Jumping jack movements in moderation (to help stone pass)\"]', 'Start the day with horse gram water, stay hydrated throughout the day, and maintain regular physical movement.', '7-8 hours of sleep; avoid sleeping late which drys body channels.', 'Gentle breathing exercises.', '[\"Vata\",\"Kapha\"]', '[\"Kidneys\",\"Ureters\",\"Urinary Tract\"]', 'Adults', 'All', 0, 0, 'High', 'Varies by individual and stone size (typically 2-4 weeks to pass small stones)', 'If back pain becomes severe and debilitating, or if you experience vomiting or blood in urine.', 'Inability to pass urine, accompanied by severe flank pain, high fever, and vomiting, indicating complete urinary obstruction.', 85, '[{\"answer\":\"Kulthi has specific lithotriptic (stone-breaking) and diuretic properties. It helps dissolve calcium oxalate crystals and flushes them out safely.\",\"question\":\"Why is Kulthi (Horse gram) good for kidney stones?\"}]', '[\"Sushruta Samhita Nidana Sthana (Ashmari Nidana)\",\"Ashtanga Hridaya\"]', 'Urologist', '[\"uti\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1579684385127-1ef15d508118?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1579684385127-1ef15d508118?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.80', 420, 90, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-4', 'Migraine', 'migraine', 'Migraine', '[\"Ardhavabhedaka\"]', 'Mental Wellness', 'Neurological Headaches', 'A neurological condition causing throbbing one-sided headaches, matching Ardhavabhedaka in Ayurveda, involving Vata-Pitta imbalances.', 'In Ayurveda, Migraine is classified as Ardhavabhedaka, meaning \'pain in half of the head\'. It is caused by aggravated Vata and Pitta doshas. High mental stress or irregular digestion produces toxins that block head channels, creating sharp vascular spasms.', '[\"Irregular sleeping patterns\",\"Skipping meals and eating acidic foods\",\"Overexposure to direct sunlight or bright screens\",\"Suppression of natural urges (Vegadharana)\"]', '[\"One-sided throbbing head pain\",\"Sensitivity to light and sound (Photophobia)\",\"Nausea and occasional vomiting\",\"Visual disturbances (Aura)\"]', '[\"Neck stiffness\",\"Yawning frequently\",\"Irritability\"]', '[\"Severe disabling headache\",\"Throbbing sensation behind eyes\",\"Temporary vision spots\"]', '[\"High stress environment\",\"Sleep deprivation\",\"Hormonal fluctuations\",\"Caffeine withdrawal\"]', '[\"Chronic migraine (more than 15 days/month)\",\"Medication overuse headache\"]', '[\"Eat meals at consistent timings\",\"Ensure regular sleep cycles\",\"Avoid direct hot sun exposure\"]', '[\"Apply sandalwood and camphor paste on forehead\",\"Drink fresh coconut water in the afternoon\"]', 'Nasya therapy (medicated oil nasal drops), Shirodhara (warm herbal oil dripping on forehead), and cooling herbs to soothe Pitta and grounding therapies for Vata.', 'Triptans, pain relievers, preventive beta-blockers, and lifestyle triggers avoidance.', '[\"Brahmi (Bacopa monnieri)\",\"Godanti Bhasma\",\"Yashtimadhu (Licorice)\",\"Ashwagandha\"]', '[\"Pathyadi Kadha\",\"Shirashooladi Vajra Ras\",\"Anu Taila (for Nasya)\"]', '[\"Sweet juicy fruits like melons\",\"Cow\'s Ghee\",\"Cardamom-spiced milk\",\"Soaked almonds\",\"Whole wheat bread\"]', '[\"Fermented foods\",\"Spicy pickles and chillies\",\"Aged cheese and sour curd\",\"Caffeine and alcohol\"]', '[\"Anulom Vilom Pranayama\",\"Shavasana\",\"Bhramari Pranayama\"]', '[\"Moderate evening walks\",\"Gentle stretching exercises\"]', 'Maintain a strict sleep schedule, massage soles of feet with warm sesame oil before bed, and take warm water in the morning.', '7-8 hours of sleep; avoid late-night screen usage.', 'Practice deep breathing (Pranayama) and quiet meditation in a dark room.', '[\"Vata\",\"Pitta\"]', '[\"Head\",\"Nerves\",\"Vascular System\"]', 'Adults', 'All', 1, 0, 'Moderate', 'Varies by individual and severity (typically 1-2 months for significant reduction in episodes)', 'If headache is sudden and explosive (\'thunderclap\'), or accompanied by weakness on one side of the body.', 'Sudden onset of headache with high fever, neck stiffness, confusion, or speech difficulties.', 90, '[{\"answer\":\"The nose is the doorway to the head. Nasya clears local sinus channels, lubricates nerve endings, and reduces cranial tension, preventing spasm triggers.\",\"question\":\"Why does Nasya help in migraines?\"},{\"answer\":\"While caffeine may provide temporary relief by constricting blood vessels, chronic intake can lead to withdrawal headaches and aggravate Pitta.\",\"question\":\"Can I drink coffee to relieve my migraine?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Siddhi Sthana\",\"Bhaijajya Ratnavali\",\"European Journal of Neurology Guidelines\"]', 'Ayurveda Mind & Nerve Specialist', '[\"anxiety\",\"insomnia\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506126613408-eca07ce68773?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506126613408-eca07ce68773?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.80', 390, 85, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-5', 'Psoriasis', 'psoriasis', 'Psoriasis vulgaris', '[\"Kitibha Kushtha\",\"Ekakushtha\"]', 'Skin Disorders', 'Dermatological Imbalances', 'A chronic autoimmune skin condition causing scaling and inflammation, understood as Kitibha Kushtha in Ayurveda, involving Vata-Kapha.', 'In Ayurveda, Psoriasis is known as Kitibha Kushtha. It is a Vata-Kapha skin disorder caused by blood (Rakta) and lymphatic (Lasika) impurities. It often originates from poor food combinations (Viruddha Ahara), which create deep metabolic toxins (Amavisha) that manifest on the skin.', '[\"Incompatible food combinations (e.g., milk and fish, citrus fruits and milk)\",\"Excessive intake of sour, salty, and heavy food\",\"Suppression of natural urges (vomiting, bowel movements)\",\"Severe psychological stress\"]', '[\"Silvery scale patches on the skin\",\"Severe skin itching and burning\",\"Dry, cracked skin that may bleed\",\"Inflamed, reddish skin plaques\"]', '[\"Small dry reddish papules\",\"Mild scaling on elbows or scalp\"]', '[\"Systemic skin peeling\",\"Joint pain (Psoriatic arthritis)\",\"Thickened, pitted nails\"]', '[\"Stressful life events\",\"Incompatible food habits\",\"Cold weather exposure\",\"Family history\"]', '[\"Psoriatic Arthritis\",\"Secondary skin infections\",\"Cardiovascular risks due to chronic inflammation\"]', '[\"Avoid incompatible food pairings\",\"Moisturize skin with natural oils regularly\",\"Avoid harsh chemical soaps and detergents\"]', '[\"Apply organic coconut oil mixed with camphor\",\"Drink water stored in copper vessels\"]', 'Detoxification therapies like Vamana (induced emesis) and Virechana (purgation) to purify the blood, followed by regular applications of neem and turmeric formulations.', 'Topical corticosteroids, coal tar preparations, phototherapy, and systemic immunosuppressive drugs or biologics.', '[\"Neem (Azadirachta indica)\",\"Manjistha (Rubia cordifolia)\",\"Khadir\",\"Haridra (Turmeric)\"]', '[\"Kaishore Guggulu\",\"Panchanimbadi Churna\",\"777 Oil (Wrightia tinctoria formulation)\"]', '[\"Bitter vegetables (Gourd, Neem leaves)\",\"Mung dal\",\"Boiled warm water\",\"Spelt and oats\",\"Pomegranate\"]', '[\"Yoghurt and sour curd\",\"Citrus fruits\",\"Fermented foods and alcohol\",\"Fish and milk combinations\",\"Processed and bakery items\"]', '[\"Pranayama (Sheetali and Bhastrika)\",\"Shavasana\",\"Vakrasana\"]', '[\"Light stretching\",\"Outdoor walking in mild sunlight\"]', 'Bathe in warm water infused with neem leaves, apply pure coconut oil immediately after bathing, and manage stress through meditation.', '7-8 hours of sleep; avoid day sleep which increases Kapha and skin impurities.', 'Mindfulness meditation and breathing techniques to control stress triggers.', '[\"Vata\",\"Kapha\",\"Pitta\"]', '[\"Skin\",\"Scalp\",\"Nails\",\"Joints\"]', 'All', 'All', 0, 0, 'High', 'Varies by individual and severity (typically 3-6 months of intensive therapy)', 'If skin plaques spread rapidly, crack and bleed, or if joint pain begins.', 'Systemic red peeling skin over the entire body (Erythrodermic psoriasis) accompanied by fever and chills.', 85, '[{\"answer\":\"Curd is sour, heavy (Abhishyandi), and clogs body micro-channels, leading to blood impurities and skin inflammation.\",\"question\":\"Why is curd restricted in Psoriasis?\"},{\"answer\":\"No, Psoriasis is an autoimmune condition. It does not spread by touch or physical contact.\",\"question\":\"Is Psoriasis contagious?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Chikitsa Sthana (Kushtha Chikitsa)\",\"Sushruta Samhita Nidana Sthana\",\"American Academy of Dermatology Guidelines\"]', 'Ayurveda Skin Specialist', '[\"arthritis\",\"anxiety\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1629909613654-28e377c37b09?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1629909613654-28e377c37b09?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.80', 450, 125, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-6', 'Obesity', 'obesity', 'Obesity', '[\"Sthoulya\",\"Medoroga\"]', 'Lifestyle Diseases', 'Metabolic Disorders', 'Excess body fat accumulation compromising health, matching Sthoulya in Ayurveda, involving Kapha dosha and Meda Dhatu.', 'In Ayurveda, Obesity is called Sthoulya or Medoroga. It is a metabolic disorder where the fat tissue channel (Meda Vaha Srotas) becomes blocked. This leads to nourishment being converted only into fat tissue (Meda), leaving other tissues like bone and muscle undernourished, due to a sluggish tissue fire (Meda Dhatvagni).', '[\"Overeating and high intake of sweet, cold foods\",\"Lack of physical exercise (Avyayama)\",\"Daytime sleeping (Divaswapna)\",\"Genetic predispositions\"]', '[\"Shortness of breath on mild exertion\",\"Excessive sweating (Sweda Adhikya)\",\"Lethargy and constant fatigue\",\"Constant hunger and sweet cravings\"]', '[\"Increase in waist circumference\",\"Mild heaviness in body\",\"Laziness\"]', '[\"Mobility limitations\",\"Severe joint pain\",\"Sleep apnea\"]', '[\"Sedentary lifestyle\",\"High calorie junk food diet\",\"Endocrine disorders\",\"Stress eating\"]', '[\"Type 2 Diabetes\",\"Hypertension\",\"Cardiovascular diseases\",\"Osteoarthritis\"]', '[\"Eat light, warm, and spicy foods\",\"Incorporate daily exercise\",\"Avoid cold drinks and sleeping during the daytime\"]', '[\"Drink warm water with organic honey and lemon on empty stomach\",\"Drink ginger and cinnamon tea\"]', 'Dry herbal powder body massage (Udvartana) to break down subcutaneous fat, scraping enemas (Lekhana Basti), and digestive herbs to activate liver metabolism.', 'Dietary calorie restriction, behavioral counseling, increased physical activity, and bariatric surgery in severe cases.', '[\"Guggulu (Commiphora mukul)\",\"Triphala\",\"Vrikshamla (Garcinia cambogia)\",\"Ginger\"]', '[\"Medohar Guggulu\",\"Triphala Guggulu\",\"Varunadi Kadha\"]', '[\"Barley (Yava)\",\"Millets like ragi and jowar\",\"Mung dal\",\"Honey (old)\",\"Spices like black pepper and ginger\"]', '[\"Cold water\",\"Sweets and ice creams\",\"Deep fried items\",\"Excess wheat and rice\",\"Heavy dairy products\"]', '[\"Surya Namaskar\",\"Kapalbhati Pranayama\",\"Trikonasana\"]', '[\"Cardio exercises (running/brisk walking)\",\"HIIT training\"]', 'Wake up by 5:30 AM, perform brisk exercise, avoid sitting for long periods, and eat dinner by 7 PM.', '6-7 hours of night sleep; absolutely no sleeping during the day.', 'Active hobbies, meditation, and mindful eating exercises.', '[\"Kapha\"]', '[\"Adipose Tissue (Meda Dhatu)\",\"Liver\",\"Heart\",\"Joints\"]', 'Adults', 'All', 0, 0, 'Moderate', 'Varies by individual (typically 3-6 months for lifestyle re-alignment)', 'If BMI exceeds 30, or if obesity is accompanied by high blood pressure or breathlessness.', 'Sudden chest pain, extreme difficulty breathing, or severe swelling in one leg.', 85, '[{\"answer\":\"Old honey has a scraping (Lekhana) quality in Ayurveda. It helps cut through excess Kapha and fat tissues, unlike fresh honey which is nourishing.\",\"question\":\"Why is old honey recommended for weight loss?\"},{\"answer\":\"No, dietary management (Ahara) is the primary pill in Ayurveda. External treatments must be supported by correct food choices to reset Agni.\",\"question\":\"Can I lose weight without changing my diet in Ayurveda?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Sutra Sthana (Ashtau Nindita Adhyaya)\",\"Sharangdhara Samhita\",\"World Health Organization Obesity Guidelines\"]', 'Ayurveda Obesity Specialist', '[\"diabetes\",\"arthritis\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512428559087-560fa5ceab42?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512428559087-560fa5ceab42?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.80', 520, 160, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-7', 'Asthma', 'asthma', 'Bronchial Asthma', '[\"Tamaka Shwasa\"]', 'Respiratory Disorders', 'Pulmonary Imbalances', 'A chronic inflammatory condition of the airways causing wheezing and breathlessness, known as Tamaka Shwasa in Ayurveda.', 'In Ayurveda, Asthma is called Tamaka Shwasa. It originates in the stomach (Amashaya), where weak digestion produces toxic mucus. This phlegm travels up and clogs the breath channel (Prana Vaha Srotas), causing Vata to become trapped and produce severe respiratory spasms.', '[\"Exposure to dust, smoke, and pollen\",\"Eating cold, heavy, and sticky foods (e.g., bananas, curd)\",\"Exposure to cold air and dry drafts\",\"Underlying digestive weakness\"]', '[\"Wheezing sound during breathing\",\"Chest tightness and congestion\",\"Shortness of breath (Shwasa Krichhrata)\",\"Dry spasmodic cough\",\"Difficulty sleeping due to coughing\"]', '[\"Dryness in throat\",\"Mild chest heaviness\",\"Sneezing\"]', '[\"Severe breathlessness even at rest\",\"Inability to speak in full sentences\",\"Cyanosis (bluish lips/face)\"]', '[\"Allergies\",\"Family history of asthma\",\"Air pollution exposure\",\"Frequent respiratory infections\"]', '[\"Respiratory failure\",\"Chronic fatigue\",\"Permanent airway remodeling\"]', '[\"Keep body warm, especially the chest\",\"Avoid cold drinks and foods\",\"Avoid exposure to dust and pollens\"]', '[\"Drink warm water with ginger and honey\",\"Inhale steam with eucalyptus oil\"]', 'Vamana (therapeutic emesis) to clear chest mucus, light warming chest massages (Uro Snehana), and lung-rejuvenating herbs (Rasayana) to strengthen the bronchial tree.', 'Inhaled corticosteroids, bronchodilators, leukotriene modifiers, and emergency rescue inhalers.', '[\"Vasa (Adhatoda vasica)\",\"Kantakari\",\"Tulsi\",\"Trikatu (Ginger, Black pepper, Long pepper)\"]', '[\"Shwasakuthar Ras\",\"Agastya Haritaki Rasayana\",\"Kanakasava\"]', '[\"Warm vegetable soups\",\"Rice with cumin\",\"Ginger tea\",\"Warm water\",\"Garlic-infused dishes\"]', '[\"Cold water and ice cream\",\"Curd and yoghurt\",\"Bananas and citrus\",\"Heavy fried foods\",\"Carbonated beverages\"]', '[\"Bhastrika Pranayama\",\"Nadi Shodhana\",\"Matsyasana (Fish pose)\"]', '[\"Gentle walking\",\"Deep breathing exercises\"]', 'Perform daily chest steaming, drink warm liquids throughout the day, and keep chest and throat covered in cold weather.', '7-8 hours of sleep; prop head up with extra pillows if congested.', 'Practice slow deep breathing to prevent anxiety-induced hyperventilation.', '[\"Kapha\",\"Vata\"]', '[\"Lungs\",\"Trachea\",\"Stomach (Origin)\"]', 'All', 'All', 1, 0, 'High', 'Varies by individual (Management of episodes, chronic control)', 'If rescue inhaler does not provide relief within 15 minutes, or chest retraction is visible.', 'Severe difficulty breathing, blue lips/fingers, or extreme chest tightness where walking is impossible.', 86, '[{\"answer\":\"Ayurveda teaches that poorly digested food creates thick phlegm (Kapha) in the stomach, which is carried by body channels to the lungs, clogging the airways.\",\"question\":\"Why does tamaka shwasa originate in the stomach?\"},{\"answer\":\"Yes, warm steam inhalation helps liquefy chest mucus and dilates bronchial passages safely. Avoid direct cold drafts immediately after steaming.\",\"question\":\"Is steam inhalation safe daily?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Chikitsa Sthana (Hikka-Shwasa Chikitsa)\",\"Sarangdhara Samhita\",\"Global Initiative for Asthma (GINA) Guidelines\"]', 'Pulmonologist', '[\"sinusitis\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559839734-2b71ea197ec2?w=400&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559839734-2b71ea197ec2?w=400&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.80', 420, 95, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-8', 'Gastritis', 'gastritis', 'Gastritis', '[\"Amlapitta\"]', 'Digestive Disorders', 'Gastrointestinal Imbalances', 'Inflammation of the stomach lining causing burning pain and acid reflux, matching Amlapitta in Ayurveda, involving Pitta dosha.', 'In Ayurveda, Gastritis is known as Amlapitta. It is primarily a Pitta dosha disorder where the digestive fire (Agni) becomes sour and highly acidic, irritating the mucosal lining of the stomach (Amashaya) and causing burning sensations and sour belching.', '[\"Excessive intake of spicy, sour, and fermented foods\",\"Skipping meals or eating late at night\",\"High intake of tea, coffee, and alcohol\",\"Chronic stress and anger (Pitta triggers)\"]', '[\"Burning sensation in chest and stomach (Hridaha)\",\"Sour and bitter belching\",\"Nausea and occasional vomiting\",\"Stomach bloating and flatulence\",\"Indigestion\"]', '[\"Mild acid reflux after meals\",\"Loss of appetite\",\"Salivation\"]', '[\"Stomach ulcers\",\"Dark tarry stools\",\"Vomiting blood\"]', '[\"Frequent use of pain relievers (NSAIDs)\",\"H. pylori infection\",\"Excessive alcohol/caffeinated drinks\",\"Highly stressful lifestyle\"]', '[\"Peptic ulcers\",\"Gastric bleeding\",\"Anemia due to chronic blood loss\"]', '[\"Eat meals at fixed intervals\",\"Avoid spicy, sour, and oily foods\",\"Avoid sleeping immediately after eating\"]', '[\"Drink cold milk with raw sugar\",\"Consume fennel seed water after meals\"]', 'Virechana (therapeutic purgation) to expel excess sour bile (Pitta) from the body, combined with cooling, healing mucosal-protective herbs.', 'Antacids, Proton Pump Inhibitors (PPIs), H2 blockers, and antibiotics for H. pylori infection.', '[\"Amalaki (Phyllanthus emblica)\",\"Yashtimadhu (Licorice)\",\"Shatavari\",\"Aloe Vera\"]', '[\"Avipattikar Churna\",\"Kamdudha Ras\",\"Sutashekhar Ras\"]', '[\"Boiled rice with coconut milk\",\"Pomegranate juice\",\"Mung dal soup\",\"Fennel seed water\",\"Cucumber\"]', '[\"Vinegar and tomatoes\",\"Red chillies and garlic\",\"Fermented batters\",\"Sour curd and pickles\",\"Citrus fruits\"]', '[\"Sheetali Pranayama\",\"Vajrasana (after meals)\",\"Shavasana\"]', '[\"Gentle walking\",\"Mild stretching\"]', 'Eat lunch between 12-1 PM (peak Pitta time), maintain a calm mind during meals, and avoid drinking water immediately before or after eating.', '7-8 hours of sleep; sleep on your left side to prevent acid reflux.', 'Cooling breathing exercises and meditation to soothe mental heat and stress.', '[\"Pitta\"]', '[\"Stomach\",\"Esophagus\",\"Duodenum\"]', 'All', 'All', 1, 0, 'Moderate', 'Varies by individual (typically 2-4 weeks with strict diet)', 'If stomach pain is persistent, or if you experience dark tarry stools or vomiting.', 'Vomiting blood (bright red or coffee grounds) or sudden severe, sharp stomach pain.', 89, '[{\"answer\":\"Licorice root (Yashtimadhu) has natural demulcent properties. It coats the stomach lining, promoting mucosal healing and buffering excess stomach acid.\",\"question\":\"Why is Licorice good for Gastritis?\"},{\"answer\":\"No, sour curd should be avoided as it is acidic and increases Pitta. Fresh, sweet buttermilk (Takra) churned with cumin is beneficial instead.\",\"question\":\"Can I eat curd when I have acidity?\"}]', '[\"Madhav Nidana (Amlapitta Nidana)\",\"Bhaijajya Ratnavali\",\"American Gastroenterological Association Guidelines\"]', 'Gastroenterologist', '[\"anxiety\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519494026892-80bbd2d6fd0d?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519494026892-80bbd2d6fd0d?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.90', 470, 130, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36'),
  ('dis-9', 'Insomnia', 'insomnia', 'Insomnia', '[\"Anidra\",\"Nidranasha\"]', 'Mental Wellness', 'Sleep Disorders', 'A sleep disorder characterized by difficulty falling or staying asleep, matching Anidra in Ayurveda, involving Vata dosha.', 'In Ayurveda, Insomnia is known as Anidra. It is caused by an aggravation of Vata dosha and a depletion of Tarpaka Kapha (the lubricating fluid in the brain). Elevated Vata (wind energy) keeps the mind hyperactive, preventing the natural heaviness of Kapha required to fall asleep.', '[\"High mental stress and overthinking\",\"Irregular sleep schedule and late-night work\",\"Excessive intake of tea, coffee, and stimulants\",\"Sleeping in an uncomfortable, noisy environment\"]', '[\"Difficulty falling asleep at night\",\"Waking up frequently during the night\",\"Waking up unrefreshed (tiredness)\",\"Daytime drowsiness and irritability\"]', '[\"Tossing and turning in bed\",\"Mild headache in the morning\",\"Lack of concentration\"]', '[\"Chronic fatigue\",\"Cognitive lapses\",\"Severe mood disturbances\"]', '[\"Stressful occupation\",\"Frequent travel across timezones\",\"Anxiety disorders\",\"Excessive blue-light exposure\"]', '[\"Impaired memory\",\"Weakened immune system\",\"Increased risk of accidents\",\"Depression\"]', '[\"Maintain a strict bedtime routine\",\"Limit screen use 2 hours before bed\",\"Avoid heavy dinners and stimulants at night\"]', '[\"Drink warm milk with a pinch of nutmeg and cardamom before bed\",\"Massage soles of feet with warm sesame oil\"]', 'Shirodhara (pouring warm herbal liquids on forehead) to calm the nervous system, Abhyanga (warm oil body massage), and adaptogenic sleep herbs.', 'Cognitive Behavioral Therapy for Insomnia (CBT-I), sleep hygiene education, and temporary use of sedative-hypnotic medications.', '[\"Ashwagandha\",\"Jatamansi\",\"Brahmi\",\"Tagar (Valerian root)\"]', '[\"Tagaradi Churna\",\"Ashwagandharishta\",\"Brahmi Vati\"]', '[\"Warm buffalo milk\",\"Oatmeal\",\"Sweet almonds\",\"Mashed rice with Ghee\",\"Dates and bananas\"]', '[\"Caffeine and carbonated beverages\",\"Dry, crunchy snacks (popcorn, crackers)\",\"Spicy food at dinner\"]', '[\"Shavasana (Corpse pose)\",\"Chandra Bhedi Pranayama\",\"Balasana (Child\'s pose)\"]', '[\"Gentle yoga\",\"Light evening walks\"]', 'Maintain a calm environment in the evening, massage temples with warm oil, and turn off all bright lights after 9 PM.', '7-8 hours of sleep; maintain consistent sleep and wake-up times.', 'Mindfulness meditation and journaling thoughts before bed to clear the mind.', '[\"Vata\",\"Kapha\"]', '[\"Nervous System\",\"Brain (Majja Dhatu)\",\"Mind\"]', 'All', 'All', 1, 0, 'Low', 'Varies by individual (typically 1-3 weeks with proper sleep hygiene)', 'If sleep difficulties last more than a month and disrupt daytime performance.', 'Severe cognitive disorientation, hallucinations, or severe clinical depression due to extreme sleep deprivation.', 92, '[{\"answer\":\"Buffalo milk is naturally heavier (has more Tamas/calming properties) than cow milk, helping ground Vata and inducing natural, deep sleep.\",\"question\":\"Why is buffalo milk recommended for sleep in Ayurveda?\"},{\"answer\":\"No, blue light from screens suppresses melatonin secretion and excites Vata dosha, making it harder for the mind to settle.\",\"question\":\"Can I watch TV while trying to fall asleep?\"}]', '[\"Charaka Samhita Sutra Sthana (Ashtaunindita)\",\"Sarangdhara Samhita\",\"American Academy of Sleep Medicine Guidelines\"]', 'Ayurveda Mind & Sleep Specialist', '[\"anxiety\",\"migraine\"]', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540555700478-4be289fbecef?w=500&q=80', '[\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540555700478-4be289fbecef?w=500&q=80\"]', '[]', '4.80', 310, 75, '2026-10-02 07:04:36', '2026-10-02 07:04:36');

